    "description": {
      "chat": "",
      "gmnotes": "",
      "short": "",
      "unidentified": "",
      "value": "<p>By simply speaking aloud, you can alter reality to better suit you. Even&nbsp;wish, however, has its limits. A&nbsp;wish&nbsp;spell can produce any one of the following effects.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Duplicate any technomancer spell of 6th level or lower.</li>\n<li>Duplicate any other spell of 5th level or lower.</li>\n<li>Undo the harmful effects of certain spells, such as&nbsp;feeblemind.</li>\n<li>Produce any effect whose power level is in line with the above effects.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>At the GM’s discretion, you may try to use a wish to produce greater effects than these, but doing so may be dangerous or the spell may have only a partial effect.</p>\n<p>A duplicated spell allows saving throws and spell resistance as normal, but the save DCs are the same as for a 7th-level spell. For the purpose of other effects that depend on spell level,&nbsp;wish&nbsp;counts as a 9th-level spell.</p>"
    },
